"file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069892/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed0c4c2b27f649db0e06117faf26a11fa1dc0422ff972c3fcc638a892804135"} {"question" "q-334106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nLet's now sketch the phase portrait.\n\n- First, notice that ${x}_{E}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ are the equilibrium solutions of the system since ${x}_{E}^{′}(t)=0.$ These solutions form the line with the equation $y=x$ in the phase space, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069892/assets/18fad31b9f69e55d9f4bc414d3e1b732eaee7685bf36a183033fc302e911eb82.png)\n\n- Now, the line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n$y=-x$\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. Since ${e}^{-2t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069892/assets/40b02cfc27ab7bc7bcc4a76523e106066b6ed6f56c184c7bd1f59a0cd1dcfc27.png)\n\nAll other non-equilibrium solutions are parallel to the vector ${v}_{2}.$ So, the phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069892/assets/5c35d385e4ce7496a5fbbcbd344ce04583f7eaf8356e1a76a15625b77df75121.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/dif